      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2009. Published by Elsevier Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "Aimed at the chemotherapy of chronic pain two kinds of analgesic pharmacophores, substituted purine and Gly-AA-OBzl, were coupled via a five-step-reaction procedure and 19 novel conjugates N-[2-chloro-9-(tetrahydropyran-2-yl)-9H-purin-6-yl]-N-cyclopropylglycylamino acid benzylesters were provided. On mouse-tail flick model their in vivo analgesic activities were assayed. The results indicate that introducing Gly-OC(2)H(5) into the 6-position of the substituted purine leads to ambiguous increase of the analgesic activity, while introducing Gly-AA-OBzl into this position leads to significant increase of the analgesic activity."
      },
